{title: Joy to the World}
{lyricist: Isaac Watts}
{composer: Lowell Mason}
{year: 1719}
{meta: tune-year 1839}
{key: D}
{time: 2/4}
{meta: tune ANTIOCH}
{meta: meter CM (8.6.8.6) with repeats}
{meta: variation The carol, sung to ANTIOCH}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags Christmas, Advent}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Joy to the [G]world! [A]The Lord is [D]come;
Let [D]earth re[G]ceive her [A]King; [D]
Let every heart prepare Him room,
And heaven and nature [A]sing,
And heaven and nature [D]sing,
And [D]heaven, and [G]heaven, [D]and [A]nature [D]sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Joy to the [G]earth! [A]The Savior [D]reigns;
Let [D]men their [G]songs em[A]ploy; [D]
While fields and floods, rocks, hills, and plains
Re[D]peat the sounding [A]joy,
Re[A]peat the sounding [D]joy,
Re[D]peat, re[G]peat, [D]the [A]sounding [D]joy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]No more let [G]sins [A]and sorrows [D]grow,
Nor [D]thorns in[G]fest the [A]ground; [D]
He comes to make His blessings flow
Far as the curse is [A]found,
Far as the curse is [D]found,
Far [D]as, far [G]as, [D]the [A]curse is [D]found.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]He rules the [G]world [A]with truth and [D]grace,
And [D]makes the [G]nations [A]prove [D]
The glories of His righteousness,
And wonders of His [A]love,
And wonders of His [D]love,
And [D]wonders, [G]wonders, [D]of [A]His [D]love.
{end_of_verse}
